    "result": "Perfect! All tests are now passing. Here's what I fixed:\n\n1. **APPROVAL_STATUSES export** (src/finetune/index.js): The test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it wasn't being exported. I added a named export statement to expose `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` alongside the default export.\n\n2. **Toxicity metric scoring** (src/eval/index.js): The `runEvaluations` function was passing both outputs and references to all metrics. However, `toxicityMetric` only needs outputs (it has a default value for the second parameter `bannedTerms`). When it received references as the second argument, they were incorrectly treated as banned terms, causing valid outputs to be flagged. I fixed this by checking each metric function's `length` property and only passing the arguments it actually requires.\n\nAll 28 tests now pass across 8 test files.",
